    <GaugingStation location="Beversham" name="Ore" number="35004">
        <Comments>
            <Comment type="Station Summary">Compound crump weir gauging a rural catchment with clay and Chalk bedrock. Flows affected by some artificial influences.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Hydrometric">Drowning starts below QMED and has significant impact on flows, occasionally drowns as a result of d/s weed growth and siltation. One rating applied across period of record.</Comment>
            <Comment type="General">A compound Crump weir with low flow notch and crest tapping.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow record">No POT data are presented for this station as they have no non-modular flow correction applied. AMAX data have been corrected, but in some cases can be below the daily flow as these are not corrected. Full period of record peak flow data reviewed and released in September 2019 (WINFAP Files v8).</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow regime">Industrial/agricultural abstraction or gw causes a moderate reduction in natural runoff.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Catchment">Gw-influenced regime, gw catchment exceeds topographic catchment. Predominantly clay and Chalk bedrock overlain with Boulder Clay and sand and gravel. Rural, predominantly arable land.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Factors affecting runoff">GI</Comment>
        </Comments>
        <Usages>
            <Usage notes="Gaugings support deviation from the rating to adjust for non-modular conditions up to QMED." suitable="Yes" type="QMED"/>
            <Usage notes="Rating and adjustment for non-modularity unconfirmed by gaugings at very high flows." suitable="No" type="Pooling"/>
        </Usages>
    </GaugingStation>
